 cfDNA levels, we used a cutoff value of 117.8&#x02009;ng&#x02009;ml<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>, which is equal to the mean&#x0002b;2s.d. of the control value (value in HCV carriers without HCC).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Independent risk factors for OS</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Variable</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HR (95&#x00025; CI)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>cfDNA</italic></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.004</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Low<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;High<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.4 (1.5&#x02013;7.6)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Tumour size</italic></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.001</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Less than 5&#x02009;cm</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;More than or equal to 5&#x02009;cm</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">3.8 (1.7&#x02013;8.5)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t2-fn1"><label/><p>cfDNA&#x0003d;cell-free DNA; CI&#x0003d;confidence interval; HCC&#x0003d;hepatocellular carcinoma; HR&#x0003d;hazard ratio; OS&#x0003d;overall survival.</p></fn><fn id="t2-fn2"><label>a</label><p>Low, less than 117.8&#x02009;ng&#x02009;ml<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>; high, more than or equal to 117.8&#x02009;ng&#x02009;ml<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Independent risk factors for cancer recurrence in distant organs</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Variable</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HR (95&#x00025; CI)</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>cfDNA</italic></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.014</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Low<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">1</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;High<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">4.5 (1.3&#x02013;14.9)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td al